From 5b4412ceb92ada0bf5827c01c108dab1f39216ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 13:02:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/17] fix(mailbox): push new-mail notifications to idling
 IMAP clients
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

go-imap answers IDLE out of the box, so clients saw the capability and used it,
but the server only starts its broadcast loop when the backend offers an update
channel. Ours did not, so an idling client was told nothing and sat until its
own timeout — advertising push while behaving worse than polling.

The IMAP backend now implements backend.BackendUpdater, and storing a message
publishes a mailbox update for its owner, so a client idling on that folder
learns about mail as it lands.

Updates are queued without blocking. A delivery must never wait on a stalled
IMAP consumer, and dropping an update only costs the push: the next poll or
SELECT still reports the message.

Folder subscription (SUBSCRIBE/LSUB), the other feature clients call
"subscription", already worked and is unchanged.

Also collapses the duplicated status counting that STATUS and the new push
both need into fillMailboxStatus.

Assisted-by: Claude Code:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Matheus Sampaio Queiroga <srherobrine20@gmail.com>
